@startuml
!include _libcpg-theme.iuml
title Deterministic parallel analysis — immutable plans, indexed reduction, ordered emission

actor "caller" as CALLER #FFE8CC
database "immutable CPG snapshot\nAST + CFG + DFG + call evidence" as CPG #DBE4FF
collections "canonical work list\n[f0, f1, ..., fn] or [p0, p1, ..., pn]" as WORK #FFF3BF
cloud "current Rayon pool\nwork stealing, bounded worker stacks" as RAYON #E5DBFF
rectangle "worker 0\nheap-owned plan" as W0 #D3F9D8
rectangle "worker 1\nheap-owned plan" as W1 #D3F9D8
rectangle "worker n\nheap-owned plan" as WN #D3F9D8
collections "indexed collect\n[plan0, plan1, ..., plann]" as COLLECT #C3FAE8
rectangle "single ordered emitter\nconnect_unique + entry/exit updates" as EMIT #FFD8A8
database "exact serial-equivalent CPG\nor ordered VF2 result batch" as RESULT #B2F2BB

CALLER --> CPG : choose serial or parallel API
CPG --> WORK : enumerate stable NodeId / slice order
WORK --> RAYON : indexed parallel iterator
RAYON --> W0 : read only
RAYON --> W1 : read only
RAYON --> WN : read only
W0 --> COLLECT : slot 0
W1 --> COLLECT : slot 1
WN --> COLLECT : slot n
COLLECT --> EMIT : deterministic sequence
CPG --> EMIT : mutable borrow begins only here
EMIT --> RESULT : same nodes, edges, and ordering

note bottom of RAYON
  No graph clone, lock, shared mutable plan,
  or input-shaped native recursion is admitted.
end note

note bottom of COLLECT
  Rayon may schedule work in any order;
  indexed collection restores input order.
end note

legend right
  |= colour |= role |
  |<#DBE4FF>| authoritative immutable evidence |
  |<#FFF3BF>| canonical work decomposition |
  |<#E5DBFF>| scheduler |
  |<#D3F9D8>| independent heap-owned computation |
  |<#C3FAE8>| deterministic reduction |
  |<#FFD8A8>| ordered mutation boundary |
  |<#B2F2BB>| exact public result |
endlegend
@enduml
